From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:10:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] wifi: ath12k: no rfkill GPIO on peach

Peach uses the WCN7850 parameters, whose rfkill pin 48 is not wired
on this module, so the firmware reported the radio hard-blocked
and the interface could not come up. Skip the rfkill config for
PCI id 0x110e, as ROCKNIX's WCN7860 parameters do (rfkill_pin 0).
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
index 262a20453..ac7ecc561 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -83,6 +83,13 @@ static int ath12k_core_rfkill_config(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	if (ath12k_acpi_get_disable_rfkill(ab))
 		return 0;
 
+	/* Peach borrows the WCN7850 parameters, whose rfkill GPIO 48
+	 * is not wired on this module: the firmware then reports the
+	 * radio hard-blocked. Stock has no Wi-Fi rfkill switch.
+	 */
+	if (ab->id.device == 0x110e)
+		return 0;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
 		ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;
 
-- 
